                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
            %p
              (adapted from
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Some+title+containing+the+words+%22homotopy%22+and+%22symplectic%22%2C+e.g.+this+one"} Ševera 00
          %h2#references References
          %p The original reference is
          %ul
            %li#AKSZ
              M. Alexandrov,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"} Maxim Kontsevich
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Schwarz"} Albert Schwarz
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oleg+Zaboronsky"} Oleg Zaboronsky
              = succeed "," do
                %em The geometry of the master equation and topological quantum field theory
              %strong 12
              7 (1997) 1405–1429 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9502010"}> arXiv:hep-th/9502010
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217751X97001031"} doi:10.1142/S0217751X97001031
          %p
            Dmitry Roytenberg wrote a useful exposition of the central idea of the original work and studied the case of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Courant+sigma-model"} Courant sigma-model
            in
          %ul
            %li#Roytenberg
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Roytenberg"}> Dmitry Roytenberg
              ,
              %em AKSZ-BV Formalism and Courant Algebroid-induced Topological Field Theories
              Lett. Math. Phys.
              %strong 79
              (2007) 143-159 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0608150"}> arXiv:hep-th/0608150
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11005-006-0134-y"} doi:10.1007/s11005-006-0134-y
          %p A similar presentation, together with a discussion about boundary conditions, can be found in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+S.+Cattaneo"}> Alberto S. Cattaneo
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"} Giovanni Felder
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the AKSZ formulation of the Poisson sigma model
              %strong 56
              (2001) 163-179 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0102108"}> arXiv:math/0102108
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1010963926853"} doi:10.1023/A:1010963926853
          %p Other reviews include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noriaki+Ikeda"}> Noriaki Ikeda
                ,
                %em Deformation of graded (Batalin-Volkvisky) Structures
                in Dito, Lu, Maeda, Weinstein (eds.)
                %em Poisson geometry in mathematics and physics
                Contemp. Math. 450, AMS (2008)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noriaki+Ikeda"}> Noriaki Ikeda
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on AKSZ Topological Field Theories for Physicists
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1204.3714"} arXiv:1204.3714
          %p A cohomological reduction of the formalism is described in
          %ul
            %li
              F. Bonechi, P. Mnëv,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Zabzine"} Maxim Zabzine
              = succeed "," do
                %em Finite dimensional AKSZ-BV-theories
              %strong 94
              (2010) 197-228 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0903.0995"}> arXiv:0903.0995
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11005-010-0423-3"} doi:10.1007/s11005-010-0423-3
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Voronov"}> Theodore Voronov
              \:
              %em Vector fields on mapping spaces and a converse to the AKSZ construction
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1211.6319"}> arxiv/1211.6319
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            That the AKSZ action on bounding manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mover
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \hat \Sigma
            is the integral of the graded symplectic form over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \Sigma
            is theorem 4.4 in
          %ul
            %li
              A. Kotov, T. Strobl,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Characteristic classes associated to Q-bundles
              %strong 12
              01 (2015) 1550006 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0711.4106v1"}> arXiv:0711.4106v1
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0219887815500061"} doi:10.1142/S0219887815500061
          %p
            The discussion of the AKSZ action functional as the
            = succeed "-functional" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroid"} symplectic Lie n-algebroid
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Weil+theory"} ∞-Chern-Weil theory
            is due discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/AKSZ+Sigma-Models+in+Higher+Chern-Weil+Theory"} AKSZ Sigma-Models in Higher Chern-Weil Theory
              %strong 10
              (2013) 1250078 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1108.4378"}> arXiv:1108.4378
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0219887812500788"} doi:10.1142/S0219887812500788
          %p
            In the broader context of smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            this is discussed in section 4.3 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+conditions"} boundary conditions
            for the AKSZ sigma model includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Bouwknegt"}> Peter Bouwknegt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Branislav+Jurco"} Branislav Jurco
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    AKSZ construction of topological open
                    = succeed "-brane" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                %strong 25
                03 (2013) 1330004 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1110.0134"}> arxiv/1110.0134
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0129055X13300045"} doi:10.1142/S0129055X13300045
            %li#IkedaXu13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noriaki+Ikeda"}> Noriaki Ikeda
                , Xiaomeng Xu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Canonical functions and differential graded symplectic pairs in supergeometry and AKSZ sigma models with boundary
                %strong 55
                (2014) 113505 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.4805"}> arXiv:1301.4805
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.4900834"} doi:10.1063/1.4900834
          %p With coisotropic boundary conditions:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theo+Johnson-Freyd"}> Theo Johnson-Freyd
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Exact triangles, Koszul duality, and coisotropic boundary conditions
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1608.08598"} arxiv/1608.08598
          %p
            An example in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+spin+gauge+theory"} higher spin gauge theory
          %ul
            %li#AlkalevGrigorievSkvortsov14
              K.B. Alkalaev, Maxim Grigoriev, E.D. Skvortsov,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Uniformizing higher-spin equations
              %strong 48
              (2015) 015401 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.6507"}> arXiv:1409.6507
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1751-8113/48/1/015401"} doi:10.1088/1751-8113/48/1/015401
          %p
            Discussion as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+functorial+field+theories"} extended functorial field theories
            via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
          %ul
            %li#CalaqueHaugsengScheimbauer2025
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Damien+Calaque"}> Damien Calaque
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"} Rune Haugseng
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudia+Scheimbauer"} Claudia Scheimbauer
              = succeed "," do
                %em The AKSZ Construction in Derived Algebraic Geometry as an Extended Topological Field Theory
              %strong 308
              1555 (2025) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.02473"}> arXiv:2108.02473
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/memo/1555"} doi:10.1090/memo/1555
        .revisedby
